# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js 16 project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` (version 2.0.1)
- **Package Manager**: npm (bun was not available in the environment)
- **Method**: Ran `npm install @vercel/analytics`

### 2. Files Modified

#### `package.json`
- Added `"@vercel/analytics": "^2.0.1"` to dependencies

#### `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after `<Toaster />`
- This follows the Next.js App Router pattern as specified in the official Vercel documentation

#### `next-env.d.ts` (auto-generated)
- Automatically updated by Next.js during build process
- Added reference to `.next/types/root-params.d.ts`

#### `package-lock.json` (new file)
- Generated npm lock file with all dependency resolutions

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.1.1 with App Router
- **Router Type**: App Router (detected via `src/app/layout.tsx`)
- **Implementation**: Used `@vercel/analytics/next` as specified for Next.js projects

### Code Changes
Following the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide, the Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) which ensures it loads on every page of the application.

The component was placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it doesn't block critical rendering.

